      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing lower leaves often signal a nutrient deficiency or uneven watering—especially nitrogen, which moves upward in the plant. Check the soil’s pH (ideal 6.0‑6.8 for tomatoes) and amend with a balanced fertilizer or compost, and water consistently so the soil stays evenly moist but not soggy. Adding a side‑dressing of well‑rotted manure or a slow‑release tomato feed can boost nitrogen, while a lime amendment will raise pH if it’s too acidic. Also mulch the beds to keep moisture steady and prevent further stress.",
